    "score_details": "Compute the Pearson correlation between the 378-element binary equality vectors for initial-class membership, and separately between the average-rank length vectors. A missing RF locus excludes the relevant point and all its initial-class pairs. Candidate length ranks are computed on the complete witness before applying the RF mask. For each score maximize over 56 alignments. Forward index k maps manuscript position i to source (i+k) modulo 28. Reverse index k maps i to 27-((i+k) modulo 28). Thus reverse index 5 maps f69v.4 to the table’s 23rd entry. NumPy random seed 69128 and 3,999 whole-name permutations hold the letter class and length of each candidate entry together. Ties count in the upper tail and the reported P adds one to its numerator and denominator.",
    "scope": "This is one-source-aware-observer work with no independent blind annotator. The historical signals are conditional on simple length or first-class preservation. The six spellings or lists and two scores per edition were exploratory, and the three transcriptions represent the same manuscript. The Henry Bate prose and quarter tests followed the initial finding. A result at the table-selected fixed shift does not substitute for an independent fixation of the shift.",
